                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>During his news conference of March 24, 1954, President Eisenhower commented on
                    the impending Geneva Conference and the battle of Dien Bien Phu. In the course
                    of his remarks, he described the Southeast Asian area as being of “the most
                    transcendent importance.”</p>
                <pb facs="1193" n="1161" xml:id="pg1161"/>
                <p>For the record of the news conference of March 24, see <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Public Papers of the Presidents of the United States: Dwight D. Eisenhower,
                        1954</hi>, pages 339–349.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
